{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe01\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Authorization inconsistency across 200 services makes local correctness insufficient.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Contain the endpoint, preserve evidence, and solicit independent local-fix, helper-audit, and systemic-escalation proposals.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Enumerate authorization paths, generate tests for bypass variants, compare helper usage, and rank proposals against observed exploitability and regression evidence.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsifiers first; select the smallest evidenced containment and fix, escalating only if cross-service evidence survives adversarial review.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Approve emergency risk posture, systemic escalation threshold, and any customer or regulator communication.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Security incident commander may halt deployment or widen containment.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record bypass class, helper coverage, failed hypotheses, and whether systemic remediation earned budget.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe02\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Two days and sparse nondeterministic failures limit causal certainty.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Instrument one failing path and solicit product-race, test-race, and infrastructure-noise explanations with disconfirming predictions.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Cluster failure traces, replay with controlled timing, vary environment and retries, and estimate hypothesis support without treating retries as resolution.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund experiments that can falsify competing causes; choose the lowest-cost explanation consistent with discriminating evidence.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Choose residual-risk acceptance and whether to quarantine, repair, or escalate the test.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The incident owner may stop experiments at the two-day boundary.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Persist timing traces, environmental contrasts, falsified causes, and confidence limits.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe03\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"40 internal consumers and three external clients must remain live during type change.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Inventory contracts and solicit expand-migrate-contract, dual-write, and compatibility-layer proposals.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Trace schemas and call sites, generate compatibility tests, replay traffic where available, and detect readers or writers that falsify each plan.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select a bounded staged migration whose rollback and compatibility claims survive consumer-specific falsification.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Approve contract versioning, external communication, migration windows, and deprecation authority.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Migration owner may pause on contract failure, data divergence, or rollback impairment.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Store dependency inventory, compatibility evidence, rollback results, and consumer sign-offs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe04\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Six changes confound attribution while full rollback sacrifices urgent fixes.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Freeze further changes and solicit per-change isolation, interaction-effect, and infrastructure-baseline proposals.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Correlate deploys with traces, segment p99 by route and cohort, replay candidate changes, and run bounded canaries with latency gates.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsifiers of each change's causal claim; select the smallest reversible mitigation meeting the latency objective.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Set acceptable latency regression and decide which urgent fixes may be temporarily constrained.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Service owner may halt canaries or restore the last safe subset.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Capture causal experiments, interaction effects, metric-quality failures, and retained-change rationale.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe05\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Security exposure competes with serialization incompatibility across 18 services.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Define exposure and compatibility gates, then solicit patch-now, adapter, and staged-upgrade proposals.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Inventory serialized contracts, differential-test old and new versions, scan reachable vulnerable paths, and run canary interoperability checks.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund tests designed to break compatibility and security assumptions; choose the bounded path minimizing evidenced combined risk.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Accept residual vulnerability or compatibility risk and authorize emergency sequencing.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Security and service owners may stop rollout on exploit exposure or contract breakage.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record affected contracts, failed compatibility cases, exposure evidence, and upgrade sequencing.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe06\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Silent loss lacks reconciliation and ownership, so the defect's scope is unknown.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Stop silent acceptance, preserve inputs and outputs, and solicit reconciliation, replay, and ownership-remediation proposals.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Build count and checksum controls, compare source-to-sink records, replay bounded samples, and map pipeline responsibility from observed evidence.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsifiers of the loss estimate and causal hypotheses; execute the smallest repair that makes loss observable and recoverable.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Assign accountable ownership and approve recovery or customer-impact decisions.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Pipeline owner may halt processing when integrity controls fail.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain reconciliation controls, loss taxonomy, ownership map, and recurrence budget.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe07\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Existing callers require compatibility while ambiguity must be made impossible or explicit.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Inventory caller intent and solicit overload, versioned-method, and explicit-options proposals.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Mine call patterns, generate migration warnings, test semantic edge cases, and use adversarial callers to expose remaining ambiguity.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund proposals that falsify backward-compatibility and clarity claims; select a bounded API change with a migration path.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Approve deprecation policy, semantic versioning, and exceptions for unusual callers.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"SDK owner may stop rollout on caller breakage or renewed ambiguity.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Document intent patterns, defect-preventing constraints, migration outcomes, and retained compatibility debt.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n01\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"30 mechanisms and 400 overlapping papers exceed the capacity for broad validation.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Define conductivity-loss discriminators and solicit heterogeneous experiment proposals spanning competing mechanisms.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Deduplicate evidence, extract conditions and endpoints, cluster mechanisms, and score experiments by information gain and falsifiability.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund proposals that could distinguish or falsify leading mechanisms; select three bounded experiments with nonredundant predictions.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Set acceptable uncertainty and approve tradeoffs among novelty, feasibility, and discrimination.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Experiment lead may stop a run when controls or interpretability fail.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Update mechanism weights, evidence provenance, negative results, and remaining budget.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n02\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Examples do not validate a conjecture if the graph class is misstated.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Solicit independent formalization, counterexample-search, and class-repair proposals before extending computation.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Check definitions, generate exhaustive small cases where possible, search outside the claimed class, and verify computational certificates.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsifiers of both the conjecture and its domain; execute the narrowest claim surviving formal and computational evidence.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Choose whether to publish a correction, weaken the claim, or continue investigation.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Proof owner may stop computation once the class boundary is disproven.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Version definitions, retain counterexamples, certify computations, and update conjecture scope.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n03\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Only two reversible tests are affordable and competitor response is adaptive.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Solicit opposing free-tier, no-free-tier, and information-gathering test designs with explicit falsifiers.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Model contribution, conversion, support load, and competitor-response scenarios without assigning unsupported probabilities; predefine stopping metrics.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund the two tests with greatest discrimination and bounded downside; select the winner only against observed evidence.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Set strategic risk tolerance and approve launch, stop, or pivot thresholds.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Business owner may stop either test on predefined harm or invalidation.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Update response assumptions, metric reliability, reversibility estimates, and next-test budget.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n04\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Unknown validation, data, retention, appeal, and legal conditions make definitive notice claims unsafe.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Solicit compliance, worker-impact, and minimum-disclosure drafts that expose their own unknowns.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Create an assumptions and evidence register, run consistency checks, and flag every unsupported promise or omission.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsification by legal, privacy, accessibility, and affected-worker reviewers; select only language supported by verified facts.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Supply or approve missing policy facts and accept residual compliance uncertainty.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Responsible legal or policy authority may block publication.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Maintain a versioned evidence register, unresolved questions, review decisions, and update triggers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n05\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"One instructor cannot manually individualize and assess 90 mixed-level engineers reliably.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Solicit differentiated practice, peer-supported, and machine-assisted assessment proposals with failure cases.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Place learners using observed diagnostic evidence, generate controlled practice variants, score reliability, and surface misclassification.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsifiers of assessment validity and access assumptions; execute a bounded cohort design that preserves human review.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Set mastery thresholds, accommodations, and escalation rules for disputed assessments.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Instructor may stop any exercise or assessment producing unreliable or harmful signals.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Update learner profiles, item validity, workload estimates, and allocation across support modes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n06\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Arrivals and downtime vary, while urgent samples cannot be delayed and capacity is unknown.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Map urgency and bottlenecks from observed operations, then solicit queueing, reservation, and downtime-contingency proposals.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Replay historical operational data if available, simulate scenarios without invented capacity, and test policies against urgent-sample service constraints.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsifiers under adverse arrival and downtime scenarios; select a bounded policy with visible fallback triggers.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Set clinical priority rules and approve tradeoffs for nonurgent work.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Clinical operations authority may suspend the policy when urgent service is threatened.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record observed arrival patterns, downtime effects, policy failures, and capacity evidence gaps.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n07\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Four languages and visual-access needs require convergent usability evidence, not aesthetic consensus.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Solicit multilingual, tactile, audio, and low-vision wayfinding proposals from heterogeneous designers and users.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Prototype variants, run accessibility and comprehension tests, and identify navigation failures by language and impairment.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsifiers of legibility, translation, and route-comprehension claims; select the bounded system with strongest observed access performance.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Approve cultural, clinical, and implementation tradeoffs and the final deployment scope.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Design or patient-safety authority may stop deployment on navigation risk.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Store test observations, rejected affordances, translation decisions, and post-deployment update budget.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n08\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Board compression can erase minority evidence or expose identities.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Solicit competing syntheses: majority-pattern, minority-risk, and decision-threshold views, with privacy attack reviews.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Cluster transcripts, preserve dissent and provenance, redact identifiers, detect sampling imbalance, and test claims against source excerpts.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsifiers of representativeness, privacy, and causal claims; select a bounded recommendation that exposes uncertainty and dissent.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Decide which risks and minority signals require board attention despite low frequency.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Research lead may block any synthesis that fails privacy or provenance checks.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain anonymized evidence lineage, dissent register, synthesis errors, and decision updates.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n09\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"A fast-moving field has unstable evidence and overlapping or contaminated benchmarks.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Solicit independent field maps emphasizing chronology, dataset lineage, leakage detection, and contradiction hunting.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Deduplicate papers and datasets, trace benchmark reuse, test leakage indicators, and align contradictory results by conditions and definitions.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsifiers of novelty, independence, and benchmark validity; execute a bounded map with confidence labels.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Set the map's decision use and acceptable unresolved contradiction.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Research owner may halt claims when provenance or leakage cannot be established.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Version the map, dataset graph, contradiction ledger, and monitoring budget.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n10\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Authored payoff ranges are uncertainty sets, not empirical probabilities.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Solicit evolutionary-game models using alternative payoff structures, update rules, and adversarial parameter choices.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Run sensitivity and robustness analyses, separate structural from probabilistic claims, and search for cooperation-breaking regimes.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund falsifiers across the uncertainty